            <ArticleTitle>Different Cutpoints for Transient Elastography Lead To Different Associations with Cirrhosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1542-3565(17)31405-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cgh.2017.11.032</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Our results illustrate the sensitivity of odds ratios to the transient elastography cutpoint used to define cirrhosis. Given problems with cutpoints, we recommend regression analysis with a continuous or ordinal-outcome model to obtain a summary across the variation.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 AGA Institute. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
